msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/storages.rst:139
msgid "Event isolation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/storages.rst:141
msgid "Polling processes updates as concurrent tasks, so two messages from the same user may race on one FSM cell. The ``events_isolation=`` argument of the dispatcher wraps each stateful dispatch in a lock:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/storages.rst:145
msgid ":class:`~aiorubi.fsm.storage.memory.DisabledEventIsolation` — default, no locking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/storages.rst:147
msgid ":class:`~aiorubi.fsm.storage.memory.SimpleEventIsolation` — in-process ``asyncio.Lock`` per key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/storages.rst:149
msgid ":class:`~aiorubi.fsm.storage.redis.RedisEventIsolation` — cross-process Redis lock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/storages.rst:152
msgid "The current state string is read **after** the lock is acquired, so handlers always observe a consistent ``raw_state``."
msgstr ""

